{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for the sum of all possible values of \\( f(10^{100}) \\), we start by analyzing the given equation \\( g(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\) where \\( g(x) = x^2 - 11x + 30 \\).\n\nFirst, let's express \\( g(f(x)) \\) in terms of \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[ g(f(x)) = (f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30. \\]\n\nWe know that:\n\\[ (f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30 = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42. \\]\n\nTo find \\( f(x) \\), we need to determine the roots of the polynomial \\( x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\). Let's denote the roots of this polynomial by \\( r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4 \\). Then, we have:\n\\[ (f(x) - r_1)(f(x) - r_2)(f(x) - r_3)(f(x) - r_4) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42. \\]\n\nSince \\( g(x) = (x-5)(x-6) \\), it follows that \\( f(x) \\) must be one of the roots of the polynomial \\( x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\) shifted by 5 or 6. Therefore, the possible values of \\( f(x) \\) are \\( r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4, r_1+5, r_2+5, r_3+5, r_4+5, r_1+6, r_2+6, r_3+6, r_4+6 \\).\n\n","prefix_end":940,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,279,2629,315,678,3204,2750,315,17767,282,7,16,15,47822,16,15,15,5410,1124,701,582,1191,553,41018,279,2661,23606,17767,342,955,2075,593,284,856,61,19,481,220,16,19,87,61,18,488,220,21,17,87,61,17,481,220,24,16,87,488,220,19,17,1124,8,1380,17767,342,2075,8,284,856,61,17,481,220,16,16,87,488,220,18,15,1124,3593,5338,11,1077,594,3158,17767,342,955,2075,593,1124,8,304,3793,315,17767,282,2075,8,1124,982,78045,342,955,2075,593,284,320,69,2075,96859,17,481,220,16,16,69,2075,8,488,220,18,15,13,1124,2533,1654,1414,429,510,78045,320,69,2075,96859,17,481,220,16,16,69,2075,8,488,220,18,15,284,856,61,19,481,220,16,19,87,61,18,488,220,21,17,87,61,17,481,220,24,16,87,488,220,19,17,13,1124,2533,1249,1477,17767,282,2075,8,1124,701,582,1184,311,8253,279,19703,315,279,47311,17767,856,61,19,481,220,1